B.aos=new A.U("It's warm out \u2014 why is there a jacket?","The app looks at the whole day in three parts: morning, midday and evening. If the morning or evening is cool, it adds one layer you can take off. Morning and evening mean the hour before and after you leave and get back \u2014 set both in Settings.")
B.aoq=new A.U('What does "off at noon" mean?',"That layer is for the morning and evening, but midday is too warm for it. Wear it out, take it off at noon, put it back on later.")
B.aoM=new A.U("It's afternoon, but the picture still shows the morning outfit.",'The picture is what to wear when you leave in the morning \u2014 you get dressed once a day. When it warms up, take off the layer marked "off at noon".')
B.aoj=new A.U("Why long pants on days with a jacket?","You can take off a jacket at noon, but you can't change pants. Shorts show up only when the morning and evening are warm too.")
B.aoJ=new A.U("Why three outfits?","All three are equally warm; only color, fabric and fit differ. Pick the one you like. The four colors under the picture are a palette to match with clothes you already own.")
B.aoi=new A.U('What happens when I tap "Too warm / Just right / Too cold"?','Your personal adjustment moves a little. "Too warm" means lighter clothes next time, "too cold" means warmer ones. It learns fast for the first 10 answers, then slowly. It asks once a day, in the evening.')
B.aom=new A.U("I want the app to start learning from scratch.",'Tap "Reset learning" at the bottom of Settings. Your answers are erased and it starts again from the body type you picked at the start (Runs cold / Normal / Runs warm).')
B.aon=new A.U("When do the umbrella, wind and UV signs appear?","Umbrella: chance of rain 50% or more. Wind: 30 km/h (about 19 mph) or more. UV is always shown as Low, Medium or High; on High days (UV 6+) the picture adds sunglasses while the sun is up. Under a 20% chance of rain, the sky shows cloudy instead of rain.")
B.aoU=new A.U("What are the Home / Office buttons?","They appear only if you added a work location more than 20 km from home. Tap one to see that place's weather and graph. The outfit uses work weather for midday only.")
B.aoL=new A.U("Where does my data go?","Only the coordinates for your forecast go to Open-Meteo. Place names, address search and the map also use your rough location. There is no login; your answers and settings stay on your phone.")
B.a7J=s([B.aoT,B.aos,B.aoq,B.aoM,B.aoj,B.aoJ,B.aoi,B.aom,B.aon,B.aoU,B.aoL],t.Wy)
